    cuda: measure the pinned host KV allocation properties
    
    N8 from the decode survey: the pinned KV body is one large cudaMallocHost,
    and the survey asked whether the allocation's own properties -- write
    combining, huge-page backing, NUMA affinity -- are worth anything on the
    transport side.
    
    Three opt-in, mutually exclusive modes, all no-ops unless the environment
    variable is set:
    
      GGML_CUDA_PINNED_WC      cudaHostAlloc with cudaHostAllocWriteCombined.
                               The steady-state pattern is host-write /
                               device-read, which is what write combining is
                               for; host reads of the body (state
                               serialization, prompt cache, rollback) become
                               uncached.
      GGML_CUDA_PINNED_HUGE    2 MiB-aligned posix_memalign + MADV_HUGEPAGE +
                               cudaHostRegister.
      GGML_CUDA_PINNED_NOHUGE  the same path with MADV_NOHUGEPAGE. This is what
                               makes the huge-page question answerable on a host
                               whose THP policy is already "always": HUGE
                               against NOHUGE isolates the page size from the
                               allocation path.
    
    Registered allocations are tracked so the free path can unregister them
    instead of calling cudaFreeHost.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E8bBMKTLSzVbDBSUfdQc9N

